---
title: Duck ragout linguine
servings: 20
tags: [italian, duck, weekend, make-ahead]
cuisine: italian
source: Duck Ragoût Linguine by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/duck-ragout-linguine
---

> A restaurant batch: the quantities make about 20 plates. Scale down for home.

== Duck confit ==

Grind @salt{8%oz} in a #food processor{} with a handful each of
@oregano{}(fresh), @thyme{}(fresh) and @orange peel{}(dried). Tip into a bowl
and stir in @salt{16%oz}, @sugar{8%oz} and @garlic{4%oz}(minced).

Rub the cure all over the @duck legs{10%lb} in a #hotel pan{}. Cover and
refrigerate ~{12%hours}.

Heat the oven to 325°F. Rinse off the cure, dry the legs and lay them back in
the pan. Cover with @duck fat{2.5%l}, topping up with @olive oil{} until
submerged. Cook ~{2.5%hours}, until fork-tender.

Cool, then discard the skin and pick the meat. Refrigerate in a covered tub.

== Bordelaise ==

Reduce the @chicken stock{15%l} by half in a #stockpot{} over medium heat,
skimming as it goes. Strain and set aside.

Reduce the @red wine{15%l} by half in a #large saucepan{}. Strain, return to
the pan, and add the reduced stock and a @bouquet garni{1}. Simmer until it
coats a spoon. Strain and keep covered.

== Linguine ==

Mix the @egg yolks{1.5%kg}, @eggs{550%g}, @whole milk{135%g} and
@olive oil{55%g} in a #stand mixer{} with the dough hook on medium speed until
just combined.

On low speed add the @00 flour{2.6%kg} and @sea salt{40%g}. When it comes
together, raise to medium and knead until firm but not sticky. Cover and rest
~{30%minutes}.

Roll into thin sheets and cut into linguine. Hold on trays dusted with
@semolina{}, covered.

== Vegetables ==

Melt @butter{8%oz}(cultured, cubed) in a #sauté pan{} over medium heat. Add
@thyme{3%sprigs}, @shallots{6}(very finely diced), @celery root{1}(very finely diced) and @carrots{2}(very finely diced). Cook, stirring now and then, until
tender. Season with @salt{} and @black pepper{} and set aside.

== Each plate ==

Warm 2 oz of the bordelaise in a #sauté pan{} with a spoonful of the vegetables
and some of the duck. Reduce to the thickness you like and season with
pepper. Keep warm on low.

Boil 92 g of the linguine in well-salted water ~{2.5%minutes}, until just al dente.
Drain into the pan.

Add a knob of @butter{} and toss over higher heat until the sauce emulsifies
and clings. Serve topped with fresh @oregano{}.
